VoteGA.org licensing
====================

This repository contains three kinds of material, licensed separately:

1. Original source code written for VoteGA.org (the Python data-generation
   scripts, client-side JavaScript, page templates, and workflows) — MIT
   License, Copyright (c) 2026 VoteGA.org (see below).

2. The Beautiful Jekyll theme this site is built on — MIT License,
   Copyright (c) 2023 Dean Attali (see below). Retained per the theme's terms.

3. Site content and published datasets — the written text of the pages and the
   machine-readable data files are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-
   ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0),
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/. You may share and adapt them,
   including commercially, as long as you give credit and license any adaptations
   you distribute under the same terms. Each published open-data repository also
   carries the full CC BY-SA 4.0 legalcode in its own LICENSE file and a plain-
   language NOTICE.md. The underlying facts come from public and government sources
   whose own terms may apply to anything you redistribute — see /about-the-data
   and /open-data.

